{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ve been reviewing why you came in. You had your Tysabri infusion today and then developed worsening abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. The pain started around midnight, but it got really bad this morning before the infusion. Then 15 minutes in, I felt nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And the pain is in your lower abdomen, worse on the right side, and crampy—like a squeezing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s like a vice. I’ve had pain before, but this feels more intense. And I’ve only had eight stools since last night, which is way less than normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your stools are usually watery, but now they’re softer, like ice cream, and low volume?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. And I passed two dark stools yesterday. Not bloody, but darker than usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We did an X-ray earlier, and it showed a loop of dilated small bowel on the left side—about 5.7 cm. That suggests a partial blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A blockage? But I’ve had surgeries before. Is that from scar tissue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. With your history of multiple abdominal surgeries, adhesions are a common cause. But we also have to consider your Crohn’s disease causing inflammation or a stricture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Tysabri for a few months now. I thought that was helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It may be helping overall, but flare-ups can still happen. We’ll need more imaging to see what’s going on. We’re going to do a CT scan tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Surgery is a last resort. Right now, we’re hoping this resolves with medical management. Surgery was consulted and agrees—serial exams for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. The pain is really bad. Oxycodone didn’t help much earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you IV Dilaudid, which is stronger. We’ll keep adjusting your pain meds. We also gave ondansetron for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-07-19 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want the pain to settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan from last night showed persistent inflammation in the distal ileum—about 6–7 cm thickened segment. Mild dilation just above it, but no complete obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s my Crohn’s acting up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it’s likely contributing to the partial blockage. The bowel is inflamed and narrowed, slowing things down. But no abscess or perforation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dark stools? Is there bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your stool tested negative for blood. The dark color might be from slower transit or something you ate—like the cheese last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t passed much gas either. Feels like I need to, but nothing comes out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with a partial obstruction. We’re going to place an NG tube to decompress your stomach and help relieve symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I refused it in the ER, but if it helps, okay. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-07-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use it intermittently—only when needed. It should help with nausea and bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat X-ray shows the bowel dilation is still there—about 5.3 cm—but no worsening. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. And your labs show no infection—CRP and ESR are normal, C. diff and cultures negative, CMV not detected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my kidney numbers? I saw my creatinine was up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine went from 1.1 to 1.4. Likely due to dehydration. We’ve been giving IV fluids, and it’s already back down to 1.1."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been anxious—pain makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started quetiapine and low-dose lorazepam to help. But you became a bit confused last night, so we stopped the lorazepam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did feel foggy. I’d rather be alert, even if anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-07-20 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the quetiapine and focus on pain control. We’re switching you to oral Dilaudid as you’re tolerating sips."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-07-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your NG tube has been helping. You’re passing more gas now, and your abdomen is less tender."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-07-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit better. Still sore, but not as intense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-07-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO for now, but plan to start clear liquids tomorrow if this trend continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-07-22 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re starting on clear liquids today. Your bowel sounds are better, and you passed gas overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-07-22 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Can I eat real food soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-07-22 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll advance slowly. If you tolerate liquids, we’ll try soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your MR enterography results are back. There’s a 10 cm segment of active inflammation in the distal ileum, but it’s stable compared to your last scan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No new damage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No abscess, fistula, or definite stricture. The bowel dilation has actually improved since the CT. That’s a positive sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the treatment is working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Rest, IV fluids, pain control, and bowel rest are helping. We’ll remove the NG tube today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-07-23 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m ready to get rid of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on a regular diet since yesterday and no issues. Pain is much better, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, manageable with oral meds. I’m feeling more like myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home tomorrow. You’ll go home on Percocet for breakthrough pain, same prednisone dose, and continue Tysabri monthly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another hospital stay like this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope not. Staying on Tysabri and following up with GI should help prevent flares. Your gastroenterologist’s office will call to schedule your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my anxiety?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2179-07-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking quetiapine as prescribed. Talk to your PCP if anxiety worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Vitals are stable, labs improved, and you’re walking and eating normally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discharge you in a few hours. Take Percocet only as needed, not while driving. Keep your primary care and GI follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Rest well, and call if pain returns or you can’t keep food down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2179-07-25 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-07-19 17:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-07-25 15:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of severe Crohn’s disease, status post multiple abdominal surgeries including colectomy and ileostomy takedown, was admitted with worsening abdominal pain and decreased stool frequency following a Tysabri infusion. Imaging revealed findings concerning for a partial small bowel obstruction, likely due to a combination of inflammatory stricture and adhesions. He was managed conservatively with bowel rest, NG tube decompression, IV fluids, and pain control. His renal function improved from acute kidney injury likely due to dehydration. Anxiety was managed with quetiapine after lorazepam was discontinued due to confusion. MR enterography confirmed stable active inflammation in the distal ileum without abscess or stricture. Pain resolved, diet was advanced, and he was discharged home on Percocet for breakthrough pain, continued prednisone and Tysabri, with follow-up arranged.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Acidosis",
      "Other B-complex deficiencies",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Toxic cataract",
      "Adrenal cortical steroids causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Acquired absence of intestine (large) (small)",
      "Lumbago",
      "Dehydration",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids"
    ]
  }
}
